WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.528
Hi! Today you learn the modal verbs.

2
00:00:06.928 --> 00:00:12.384
What can you do? What do you want? What must you do?

3
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:17.732
You need these four verbs every day:

4
00:00:18.132 --> 00:00:21.212
können: I can swim.

5
00:00:21.612 --> 00:00:25.100
wollen: I want to learn German.

6
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.772
müssen: I have to work.

7
00:00:29.172 --> 00:00:32.924
dürfen: you may not smoke here.

8
00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:37.473
This is how you conjugate können:

9
00:00:37.873 --> 00:00:39.945
I can

10
00:00:40.345 --> 00:00:42.417
you can

11
00:00:42.817 --> 00:00:45.657
he can, she can

12
00:00:46.057 --> 00:00:48.153
we can

13
00:00:48.553 --> 00:00:54.897
You can (formal). Note: ich and er have no ending!

14
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.536
Now an important sentence:

15
00:00:59.936 --> 00:01:02.536
I can cook well.

16
00:01:02.936 --> 00:01:10.000
The modal verb is in position two. The second verb goes to the end:

17
00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.216
He has to work today.

18
00:01:13.616 --> 00:01:20.104
It's like a bracket: kann… kochen. Muss… arbeiten.

19
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:27.064
Listen: Lena and Mateo talk about their talents.

20
00:01:27.464 --> 00:01:29.848
Can you swim?

21
00:01:30.248 --> 00:01:34.336
Yes, very well! And you?

22
00:01:34.736 --> 00:01:38.272
No, but I want to learn.

23
00:01:38.672 --> 00:01:41.368
I can show you!

24
00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:45.616
Great! On Saturday?

25
00:01:46.016 --> 00:01:48.712
I have to work then.

26
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:59.984
Now you! Say three sentences: what can you do, what do you want, what must you do today?

27
00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:15.836
Great! Now you can:

28
00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:23.588
You know the modal verbs and the verbal bracket. The second verb always goes to the end!

29
00:02:23.988 --> 00:02:26.108
See you soon!
